1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,833
Stop. Still paying just the minimum?

2
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:06,767
It keeps your account current. But debt can stick around.

3
00:00:07,067 --> 00:00:09,867
Imagine a three-thousand-dollar balance.

4
00:00:10,167 --> 00:00:13,967
At twenty-four percent A P R, interest adds up fast.

5
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:18,333
In this simplified example, the first month adds sixty dollars.

6
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:20,433
Pay one hundred dollars.

7
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:24,300
Only forty dollars reduces your original debt.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,867
Then the next month starts. And interest returns.

9
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:32,433
Keep payments fixed: one hundred versus one hundred fifty dollars.

10
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:37,533
With no new spending, that is about forty-seven months versus twenty-six.

11
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:41,467
A smaller payment today can mean a longer debt tomorrow.

12
00:00:41,767 --> 00:00:44,667
Check your A P R. Pay extra when you can.
